<section class="section-content" id="compare-travel-plans">
    <div class="il-container">
        <div class="img-list-block flex-div">
            <div class="img-block left-block width-40">
                <h2 class="heading2">How to Compare Travel Insurance Plans Online </h2>
                <figure class="mt-40">
                    <img src="/docs/default-source/assets/marketing/images/travel-images/compare-travel-insure" alt="How to Compare Travel Insurance Plans Online" title="How to Compare Travel Insurance Plans Online" class="img-right-pos">
                </figure>
            </div>
            <div class="list-block right-block width-50">
                <div class="list-block no-list">
                    <ul>
                        <li><p class="text font-16"><strong>Start With the Sum Insured:</strong> Make sure it matches your destination. Medical costs in places like the USA can escalate fast, and a low cover won’t go far.</p></li>
                        <li><p class="text font-16"><strong>Look Beyond Basic Coverage:</strong> It’s not just about medical coverage. Check whether things like trip cancellations, lost passports, missed connections or cruise interruptions are covered or not.</p></li>
                        <li><p class="text font-16"><strong>Check What You Can Add On: </strong> Not every trip is the same. If you’re planning adventure activities or renting a car, see if your travel insurance policy lets you customise your coverage with add-ons or optional covers.</p></li>
                        <li><p class="text font-16"><strong>Understand the Deductibles:</strong>What you pay out of pocket also matters. Go through the deductibles so you’re not caught off guard during a claim.</p></li>
                        <li><p class="text font-16"><strong>See How Claims Actually Work:</strong>In an emergency, the process should be simple. A digital claims journey and 24x7 international assistance can make a real difference when you’re far from home.</p></li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>


