            </div>
           
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section-content" id="calculate-travel-prem">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="img-list-block flex-div">
            <div class="img-block left-block">
                <img src="/docs/default-source/assets/product-bundle/il-travel/images/calculate-travel-insure.webp" alt="How Is Travel Insurance Premium Calculated?" title="How Is Travel Insurance Premium Calculated?" class="img-hide width-100">
            </div>
            <div class="list-block right-block org-list">
                <h2 class="heading2">How to Calculate Travel Insurance Premiums Online? </h2>
                <p class="text">You can calculate travel insurance premiums online with the help of an online calculator. Input your details, including age, pre-existing diseases, etc., choose the type of coverage needed, and select your destination to calculate premiums. Here’s how these details are used to calculate your travel insurance premium:</p>
                <ul class="mt-15">
                    <li class="text"><strong>Age of traveller:</strong> Medical risks increase with age. That’s why travel insurance premiums tend to be higher for senior travellers. </li>
                    <li class="text"><strong>Number of Travellers:</strong> A travel insurance policy covering multiple members typically has a higher premium. A family policy will have a higher premium than an individual policy. </li>
                    <li class="text"><strong>Coverage Amount:</strong> Higher sum insured means higher protection against medical and travel-related expenses. As the coverage increases, the premium also increases. </li>
                    <li class="text"><strong>Geography:</strong> Travel insurance premiums also  depend on the country or region you are travelling to. Destinations with higher healthcare costs tend to have a higher premium. </li>
                    <li class="text"><strong>Trip Duration:</strong> The longer your international trip, the higher the risk exposure. Therefore, longer travel periods generally result in higher premiums. </li>
                    <li class="text"><strong>Type of Coverage:</strong> Different travel insurance policy types have different pricing structures. For example, family travel insurance and multi-trip travel insurance may have different base rates. </li>
                </ul>
                <p class="text strong-txt mt-20">You can also refer to our travel insurance <a href="/docs/default-source/default-document-library/trip-secure-plus-calculator_v14-2.xlsb" class="link" target="_blank">rate chart.</a></p>
            </div>
           
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section-content table-block" id="factor-affect-travel">
    <div class="container">
        <h2 class="heading2 align-center">Factors That Affect Your Travel Insurance Premium</h2>
       
        <div class="table-wrapper table-auto table-style mt-30">
            <table class="table-wrap">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Factors</th>
                        <th class="no-right-border">Details</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="strong-txt">Age </td>
                        <td class="no-right-border">Older travellers are more likely to require medical assistance, which may increase the cost of travel insurance coverage.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="strong-txt">Destination</td>
                        <td class="no-right-border">Healthcare expenses and travel risks differ from one country to another. Premium tends to be higher for regions with expensive medical systems.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="strong-txt">Travel Duration</td>
                        <td class="no-right-border">Travel insurance premium is linked to the number of days you need protection. A longer journey generally means a higher premium.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="strong-txt">Number of Travellers</td>
                        <td class="no-right-border">Your premium is also calculated based on the number of individuals covered under the travel insurance policy.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="strong-txt">Sum Insured Selected</td>
                        <td class="no-right-border">Choosing a larger coverage limit increases the insurer’s liability and, in turn, the payable premium.</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="no-bottom-border strong-txt">Add-ons Opted</td>
                        <td class="no-right-border no-bottom-border">Opting for optional covers can enhance your travel insurance coverage but it can also increase your premium.</td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </div> 
</section>

<section class="section-content bg-blue-linear" id="lower-travel">
    <div class="il-container">
        <h2 class="heading2 align-center">Tips to Lower Your Travel Insurance Premium </h2>
      
        <div class="download-sec four-col owl-carousel owl-theme owl-sec">
            <div class="download-item">
                <div class="strong-no">1</div>
                <div class="down-cont">
                    <h4 class="heading4">Compare Plans Online</h4>
                    <p class="text mt-10">When you buy travel insurance online, evaluate and compare the various plans as per your needs and budget.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="download-item">
                <div class="strong-no">2</div>
                <div class="down-cont">
                    <h4 class="heading4">Choose the Right Coverage</h4>
                    <p class="text mt-10">Select the right sum insured based on your destination and trip type. Avoid over-insuring if your travel risk is limited.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="download-item">
                <div class="strong-no">3</div>
                <div class="down-cont">
                    <h4 class="heading4">Review Add-ons</h4>
                    <p class="text mt-10">Choose optional covers/add-ons that are relevant to your travel plans. This will help to avoid paying for benefits you may not require.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="download-item">
                <div class="strong-no">4</div>
                <div class="down-cont">
                    <h4 class="heading4">Consider Multi-Trip Policies</h4>
                    <p class="text mt-10">If you are fond of exploring new places across the globe, a multi-trip policy can help you save on insurance premium.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>



<section class="section-content bg-pink" id="claim-procedure">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="img-list-block flex-div">
            
            <div class="list-block left-block org-list width-50">
                <h2 class="heading2">What is the Claim Procedure for Travel Insurance Policies?</h2>
                <p class="text">Even if you have the best travel insurance policy, dealing with unpleasant incidents on your trip might be difficult if you are unaware of the claim procedure. </p>
                <ul class="mt-15">
                    <li class="text"><strong>Inform Us:</strong> To initiate a claim during an emergency on your trip, you will first need to inform us. You can call us at <a href="tel: +91 124 4498778" class="link" target="_blank">+91 124 4498778</a> or email us at <a href="mailto: icicilombard@falck.com" class="link" target="_blank">icicilombard@falck.com.</a> </li>
                    <li class="text"><strong>Submit Documents:</strong> Post intimation, you will have to provide the supporting documents related to your claim. </li>
                    <li class="text"><strong>Claim Processing:</strong> Following your submission, we will evaluate the details and the documents and come back on your claim. </li>
                    <li class="text"><strong>Track Claim:</strong> You can easily track your travel insurance claim on our website or our IL TakeCare App.</li>
                </ul>
                <p class="text strong-txt mt-20">For more information, click <a href="/travel-claims" class="link" target="_blank">here.</a></p>
            </div>
            <div class="img-block right-block width-40">
                <figure>
                    <img src="/docs/default-source/assets/product-bundle/il-travel/images/claim-procedure-travel.webp" alt="Claim Procedure for Travel Insurance Policies" title="Steps to Claim Travel Insurance" class="img-hide">
                </figure>
            </div>
            
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section-content table-block" id="document-require-travel">
    <div class="container">
        <h2 class="heading2 align-center">What are the Documents Required for Travel Insurance Claims?</h2>
        <p class="text align-center middle-width">You need to submit different documents for different categories of travel insurance claims. You can submit these documents via our website or our IL TakeCare App. </p>
        <div class="table-wrapper table-auto table-style mt-30">
            <table class="table-wrap">
                <thead>
                    <tr>
                        <th>Claim Type</th>
                        <th class="no-right-border">Documents Required</th>
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="strong-txt">Medical Expenses Claims </td>
                        <td class="no-right-border">
                            <div class="list-block disc-list">
                                <ul>
                                    <li class="text">Claim form</li>
                                    <li class="text">Flight tickets or boarding pass</li>
                                    <li class="text">Medical records, prescriptions, consultation papers.</li>
                                    <li class="text">Invoices or payment receipts</li>
                                    <li class="text">Bank account details </li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                   <tr>
                        <td class="strong-txt">Trip Cancellation Claims </td>
                        <td class="no-right-border">
                            <div class="list-block disc-list">
                                <ul>
                                    <li class="text">Claim form</li>
                                    <li class="text">Initial/unused ticket with fare</li>
                                    <li class="text">Refund/no show document issued by airline </li>
                                    <li class="text">New ticket with fare </li>
                                    <li class="text">Bank account details </li>
                                    <li class="text">Medical records, prescriptions, consultation papers (if required) </li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="strong-txt">Missed/Cancelled Flight Claims </td>
                        <td class="no-right-border">
                            <div class="list-block disc-list">
                                <ul>
                                    <li class="text">Claim form</li>
                                    <li class="text">Bank account details  </li>
                                    <li class="text">Flight tickets or boarding pass </li>
                                    <li class="text">Confirmation of delay with reason from the airline </li>
                                    <li class="text">Initial itinerary/schedule of flights </li>
                                    <li class="text">Initial/unused flight ticket with fare </li>
                                    <li class="text">Refund/no-show document issued by airline </li>
                                    <li class="text">New flight ticket with fare </li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr>
                        <td class="strong-txt no-bottom-border">Baggage Claims </td>
                        <td class="no-right-border no-bottom-border">
                            <div class="list-block disc-list">
                                <ul>
                                    <li class="text">Claim form</li>
                                    <li class="text">Bank account details  </li>
                                    <li class="text">Flight tickets or boarding pass </li>
                                    <li class="text">PIR (Property Irregularity Report) </li>
                                    <li class="text">FIR or police report or police complaint copy (if required) </li>
                                    <li class="text">Photo of the damaged baggage. </li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </td>
                    </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <p class="text align-center mt-30">For more details, please go through the policy wordings or click <a href="/travel-claims" class="link" target="_blank">here</a>. </p>
    </div> 
</section>


<section class="section-content bg-blue2-linear" id="travel-claim-rejection">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="img-list-block flex-div">
            <div class="img-block left-block width-40">
                <img src="/docs/default-source/assets/product-bundle/il-travel/images/claim-rejection.webp" alt="How to Avoid Travel Insurance Claim Rejection?" title="Must-Know Points to Avoid Travel Claim Rejection" class="img-hide width-100">
            </div>
            <div class="list-block right-block org-list width-50">
                <h2 class="heading2">How to Avoid Travel Insurance Claim Rejection?</h2>
                <p class="text">Your travel insurance claim can be rejected due to incomplete information or policy breaches. Follow these tips to avoid travel insurance claim rejections: </p>
                <ul class="mt-15">
                    <li class="text flex-col">
                        <p class="text strong-txt">Disclose Information:</p>
                        <p class="text">Provide correct details about your age, destination, travel dates and medical conditions while buying travel insurance online.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="text flex-col">
                        <p class="text strong-txt">Understand Coverage: </p>
                        <p class="text">Carefully go through inclusions and exclusions in your travel insurance policy to avoid claiming for non-covered events.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="text flex-col">
                        <p class="text strong-txt">Inform Insurer Immediately:</p>
                        <p class="text">Notify your insurance company or assistance team as soon as possible about your travel insurance claim. </p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="text flex-col">
                        <p class="text strong-txt">Gather Documents: </p>
                        <p class="text">Collect all important documents like medical bills, prescriptions, FIRs, PIRs, flight tickets or boarding pass. </p>
                    </li>
                    <li class="text flex-col">
                        <p class="text strong-txt">Follow Claim Procedure: </p>
                        <p class="text">Inform your insurer and submit documents within the stipulated time. Don’t file a claim for excluded activities.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
           
        </div>
    </div>
</section>




<section class="section-content" id="extend-travel-policy">
    <div class="il-container">
        <h2 class="heading2 align-center">Can You Extend Your Travel Insurance Policy? </h2>
        <p class="text align-center middle-width"> Yes, you can easily extend your international travel insurance policy. Just ensure you request the extension before your existing policy expires. Here’s how you can extend your policy.</p>

        <div class="no-block">
            <div class="no-item">
                <p class="number-txt">1</p>
                <p class="text">Visit our website or IL TakeCare App. You can also call us on <a href="tel: 1800 2666" class="link" target="_blank">1800 2666</a>. </p>
            </div>
            <div class="no-item">
                <p class="number-txt">2</p>
                <p class="text">Choose “Extend Existing Policy” on the website or tap on “Edit Policy Details” in the app. </p>
            </div>
            <div class="no-item">
                <p class="number-txt">3</p>
                <p class="text">Complete and acknowledge the Good Health Declaration Form. </p>
            </div>
            <div class="no-item">
                <p class="number-txt">4</p>
                <p class="text">Select the additional number of days required and pay the applicable premium to complete the process. </p>
            </div>
        </div>
        
        <a href="javascript:void(0)" class="primary-btn buy-travel-btn quote_link full-btn-width mt-40">Extend My Policy </a>
    </div>
</section>

<section class="section-content bg-pink2-linear" id="busting-common-travel">
    <div class="il-container">
        <h2 class="heading2 align-center">Busting Common Travel Insurance Myths Before Your Trip </h2>
        <div class="myth-block owl-carousel owl-theme owl-sec">
            <div class="myth-item">
                <h4 class="heading-4">Myth 1</h4>
                <p class="text strong-txt mt-10">Travel insurance only covers medical expenses </p>
                <p class="text">No, travel insurance also covers loss/delay of checked-in baggage, trip cancellation, passport loss, missed connecting flights, etc. </p>
            </div>
             <div class="myth-item">
                <h4 class="heading-4">Myth 2</h4>
                <p class="text strong-txt mt-10">Adventure sports is covered by travel insurance</p>
                <p class="text">No, travel insurance doesn’t cover risky sports unless you have purchased an optional cover that’s specifically designed to cover adventure sports.</p>
            </div>
             <div class="myth-item">
                <h4 class="heading-4">Myth 3</h4>
                <p class="text strong-txt mt-10">I don’t need travel insurance  </p>
                <p class="text">Medical emergencies and trip-related contingencies can strike anytime, anywhere. It’s better to be prepared before going on an international trip. </p>
            </div>
            <div class="myth-item">
                <h4 class="heading-4">Myth 4</h4>
                <p class="text strong-txt mt-10">Senior citizens can’t buy travel insurance policy </p>
                <p class="text">Age is just a number as anyone can buy travel insurance online. Note that ICICI Lombard offers coverage for individuals aged up to 85 years.</p>
            </div>
             <div class="myth-item">
                <h4 class="heading-4">Myth 5</h4>
                <p class="text strong-txt mt-10">I can buy travel insurance after starting my trip </p>
                <p class="text">No, you need to purchase travel insurance before going on your international trip. Note that the policy's purchase date and start date must be before you start your trip. </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

