</div><div class='sfContentBlock'><section class="section-content bg-coolgray tab-accord-sec" id="faq-sec">
    <div class="il-container">
        <h2 class="heading2 align-center">FAQs on Travel Insurance</h2>

        <div class="tab-sec">  
            <ul>
                <li class="active" id="general"><span>General</span></li>
                <li id="coverage"><span>Coverage</span></li>
                <li id="premium" class=""><span>Premium</span></li>
                <li id="claims" class=""><span>Claims</span></li>
                <li id="extension" class=""><span>Extension</span></li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="accord-wrap">
            <div class="accordian-block accord-sec" data-rel="general">
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">How does travel insurance protect me during medical emergencies abroad?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Travel insurance provides coverage for hospitalisation expenses, emergency dental treatment, medical evacuation and repatriation based on policy terms and conditions.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">What risks do Indian travellers usually overlook while travelling internationally?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Some of the commonly overlooked risks include baggage delays/loss, trip interruption, missed/cancelled flights, etc.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                  <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Is travel insurance useful even if I am travelling for a short duration?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, because travel insurance covers a range of medical and trip-related contingencies, which can happen even during short international trips.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Can one travel insurance policy cover multiple countries in a single trip?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, you just need to list all the destinations you plan to visit while buying your travel insurance policy. This ensures you’ll be covered for your entire multi-country trip.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                  <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">What happens if I travel without international travel insurance?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Travel insurance provides coverage for sudden medical expenses and travel-related losses, thereby ensuring you can travel worry-free. Besides, many countries have made travel insurance a mandatory requirement for their visa process. </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Does travel insurance offer assistance beyond medical emergencies?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, travel insurance also offers coverage for common carrier delay, damage to baggage during transit, passport loss, personal accidents and more.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">How early should I buy travel insurance before my trip?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">While it’s best to buy travel insurance as early as possible, you typically need to purchase it at least 1–2 days before your departure for the policy to be valid.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Can I buy travel insurance for parents travelling without me?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, you can purchase a travel insurance policy for parents travelling independently. Just ensure to provide all the details accurately.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Is travel insurance valid if my travel dates change after purchase?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, you can modify your travel dates after the policy purchase. You can also extend your travel policy, subject to payment of additional premium and underwriting rules.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Is travel insurance mandatory for everyone?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Travel insurance is mandatory when you want to visit certain countries (like Schengen countries). However, it is highly recommended to have travel insurance to secure yourself against travel-related risks.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Do I need to buy travel insurance for short trips as well?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes. It is always good to be insured against the unpredictable - like lost passport/baggage or medical emergency. Travel insurance will help you tackle such situations with ease.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">What happens if my travel insurance expires?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">If your travel insurance policy expires while you’re still on your international trip, then you will no longer be covered for different travel and medical-related contingencies. That’s why it is important to ensure that your travel insurance covers the entire duration of your trip abroad.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">How can I cancel my travel insurance policy?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">You can easily cancel your travel insurance before your trip start date. Just get in touch with us via our toll free number 1800 2666, email ID customersupport@icicilombard.com or the IL TakeCare App.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordian-block accord-sec" data-rel="coverage">
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Are outpatient medical expenses covered under travel insurance?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, if you opt for Outpatient Treatment for Illness and Injury Add-on. This add-on cover is available under our TripSecure+ travel insurance policy.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Will my policy cover treatment taken at non-network hospitals overseas?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, travel insurance also covers emergency treatments undertaken at non-network hospitals abroad. </p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Does travel insurance cover theft of valuables like laptops or mobile phones?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, but only if the insured member has opted for the Electronic Equipment Loss add-on. The coverage offered is subject to policy terms and conditions.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Are adventure activities automatically covered?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">No, adventure activities are only covered under the Adventure Sports add-on.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Are airline delays and missed connections covered under the policy?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, travel insurance covers common carrier delays and missed connections subject to policy terms and conditions.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Will my policy cover emergency dental treatment during travel?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, our travel insurance covers emergency dental treatment for sudden acute pain.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Does travel insurance cover baggage delay beyond a specific number of hours?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, travel insurance offers a fixed allowance when your checked-in baggage is delayed by the airline by more than six consecutive hours.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Are ambulance charges abroad covered under travel insurance?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, if the ambulance services are medically necessary and within policy limits.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Will my travel insurance cover any pre-existing disease?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Our TripSecure+ travel insurance provides coverage for pre-existing conditions via the Pre-existing disease add-on cover.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">What is accidental death coverage in travel insurance?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Under this cover, a lump sum amount is paid if the insured dies or becomes disabled while getting on, off, or traveling in a public/common carrier during the policy period.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">What is the validity period of travel insurance?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">The validity of your travel insurance depends on your trip duration. It usually starts from your date of departure and ends when you return. For more details, read the policy documents.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordian-block accord-sec" data-rel="premium">
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Why does travel insurance cost vary for different countries?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Travel insurance premium depends on the current medical costs and risk exposure in the selected travel destination.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                 <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">How does traveller age impact travel insurance pricing?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Age is one of the primary factors that affects travel insurance premium. Old age is associated with higher medical risk and therefore, it attracts a higher premium.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                 <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Does trip duration impact the final premium amount?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, longer trip duration can increase premium proportionately.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                 <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Can add-on covers increase the travel insurance premium?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, since add-ons are subject to payment of additional premium.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                 <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Is GST exemption applicable on international travel insurance premiums?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">The GST exemption is applicable to retail travel insurance policy (individual and family travel policy) – single-trip travel insurance and multi-trip travel insurance.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">How much GST do I have to pay on travel insurance premium?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">If you are buying an individual or family travel insurance policy, you don’t have to pay any GST on the premium. Earlier, 18% Goods and Services Tax (GST) was applicable but that has been removed from 22nd September 2025 by the GST Council of India.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Does the GST exemption affect my coverage?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">No, it doesn’t affect your insurance coverage. The removal of the Goods and Services Tax (GST) only reduces tax paid on the premium. So, you only pay the base premium amount and no additional taxes.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Do I have to apply or opt in to get the GST exemption?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">No, 0% GST is applied automatically when you buy a single-trip or multi-trip travel insurance policy.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordian-block accord-sec" data-rel="claims">
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Who should be informed first in case of a medical emergency abroad?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Immediately inform your insurer and 24x7 international assistance provider in case of emergencies abroad.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">What mistakes commonly lead to rejection of travel insurance claims?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Some common mistakes for claim rejection include non-disclosure of important details, incomplete documents, or claims outside policy period.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Can claims be raised digitally while travelling internationally?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, you can easily raise claims online via our website or our IL TakeCare App.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Which documents are required for baggage delay or loss claims?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">You need to submit your bank details, flight tickets/boarding pass and PIR for baggage delay-related claims. Meanwhile, for baggage loss-related claims, you just need to submit your bank details and FIR/policy complaint copy.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Can multiple claims be filed under the same travel insurance policy?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, you can file multiple valid claims under a single travel insurance policy as long as each claim falls within the policy’s coverage terms and limits.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">How long does travel insurance claim settlement usually take?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Insurers need to inform about your travel insurance claim acceptance or rejection within 7 days of receiving your claim submission.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">What happens if I exceed the sum insured during treatment abroad?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">You will have to bear the medical treatment expenses that goes beyond the sum insured.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="accordian-block accord-sec" data-rel="extension">
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Are there limits on the number of times a travel policy can be extended?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">You can extend your travel insurance policy as many times as you want. However, you can extend your policy only if the total policy is less than or equal to 360 days.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Is policy extension available for all travel insurance plans?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Yes, policy extension is available for all travel insurance policies.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="accord-row">
                    <h3 class="text strong-txt accord-title">Is a medical check-up required for extending a travel insurance policy?</h3>
                    <div class="accord-data mt-5">
                        <p class="text">Policy extension requires a Good Health Declaration.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
                
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

</div><div class='sfContentBlock'><section class="sectionSpace  section-content" id="Reviews">
    <div class="container-small">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-xs-12 text-center">
